From: Paul B Mahol <onemda@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] avcodec: add HVQM4 video decoder

The HVQM4 video decoder from Paul B Mahol's patch series "HVQM4" on ffmpeg-devel, 9 July 2023
(https://ffmpeg.org/pipermail/ffmpeg-devel/2023-July/311852.html, 0003-avcodec-add-HVQM4-video-decoder.patch),
never merged into FFmpeg, itself based on Tillmann Karras's reference decoder (https://github.com/Tilka/hvqm4,
LGPL 2.1 or later). Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later, as FFmpeg is.

Changed by Charlie Bruce for the nightfire-cxbx project, 26 October 2026 (the changes are also listed at the top of
libavcodec/hvqm4.c):
 - ported to FFmpeg 8.1 (ff_vlc_init_from_lengths, ff_vlc_free);
 - pictures decoded into contiguous Y, U and V planes as the reference decoder does, and copied out, in place of
   the padded reference AVFrames and their crop (crop_left was 64 for a 32-pixel border; right and bottom were
   never cropped);
 - every read of a reference picture checked against that picture's buffer: the reference decoder's result
   inside it, clamped outside it, where the patch skipped the rest of the macroblock;
 - Huffman trees limited to 256 leaves and 27-bit codes; one-leaf and absent trees decode without reading bits,
   as the reference decoder's do; an escape symbol from a one-leaf tree ends the sum;
 - the macroblock type and proc run lengths count as the reference decoder's do (the patch returned 0 where a
   run of 0 was decoded);
 - the nest's position, the shifts and the motion vector residual bits checked;
 - the luma run length error check tested the chroma plane's (removed: the run lengths are unsigned, as the
   reference decoder's);
 - HVQM4 1.3's chroma half-pel positions (the luma vector's) from the file header in extradata;
 - B frames, which need reordering, refused; chroma sampling other than 4:2:0 refused.
The 2022 review's points on read_trees() (no depth or leaf limit) were already met by the 2023 patch (16 levels,
256 leaves); the limit here is the VLC reader's three levels of 9 bits.
Applies to FFmpeg n8.1.3, after 0001.

